1
00:00:00,020 --> 00:00:03,460
(Sheldon:)Still sounds like a lot
of unnecessary touching.

2
00:00:03,460 --> 00:00:06,830
(Amy:)Trust me. With your right hand,
locate the spot

3
00:00:06,830 --> 00:00:09,100
(Amy:)where the scapula meets
the acromion process.

4
00:00:11,430 --> 00:00:12,130
(Sheldon:)All right.

5
00:00:12,130 --> 00:00:14,960
(Amy:)Now push your third finger along
the ridge of the shoulder blade,

6
00:00:14,960 --> 00:00:17,040
(Amy:)making a small rotation
as you do so.

7
00:00:17,040 --> 00:00:20,610
(Sheldon:)Rotating.

8
00:00:20,610 --> 00:00:22,380
(Amy:)You should feel
a small node-like object

9
00:00:22,380 --> 00:00:24,210
(Amy:)rolling back and forth along
the bone.

10
00:00:24,210 --> 00:00:26,310
(Sheldon:)You mean the myofascial point?

11
00:00:26,310 --> 00:00:29,350
(Amy:)Obviously.

12
00:00:29,350 --> 00:00:32,050
(Amy:)Now bear down on it like
the seventh grade noogies

13
00:00:32,050 --> 00:00:34,060
(Amy:)we all know too well.

14
00:00:35,720 --> 00:00:39,690
(Sheldon:)Oh, dear Lord, yes, yes,
oh, yes!

15
00:00:41,430 --> 00:00:43,530
(Sheldon:)Amy, I've never been touched
like this before!

16
00:00:45,800 --> 00:00:49,540
Oh! My hands are magic!

17
00:00:49,540 --> 00:00:51,110
(Amy:)Don't flatter yourself.

18
00:00:51,110 --> 00:00:53,470
(Amy:)Your hands are blunt tools
guided by my knowledge

19
00:00:53,470 --> 00:00:54,710
(Amy:)of the nervous system.

20
00:00:54,710 --> 00:01:00,020
(Amy:)I could just as easily have
paralyzed you.

